cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TilTale in your research, please cite it as below, with the
  version you used. Each release has its own DOI on Zenodo; the DOI below
  always points to the newest version.
type: software
title: TilTale
abstract: >-
  TilTale is an authoring tool for interactive digital narratives: branching
  stories with photos, speech bubbles and choices, made for research studies.
  Researchers and students without programming experience build a story in a
  local studio in the browser, play-test and stress-test it themselves, and
  export it as a self-contained website that runs on any web host with PHP.
  Once loaded, the story keeps working on an unstable or absent internet
  connection: events are queued on the device and sent when the connection
  returns. A participant ID from a survey or recruitment platform such as
  Qualtrics or Prolific enters through the story link and is passed back
  through a redirect when the story ends, so story logs can be linked to survey
  data. Each visit is logged per participant, and the logs can be encrypted
  on the server with a project key pair, so that only the holder of the
  private key can read them.
